# AI Slop Gate - Trivy Ignore List
# Policy: Ignore vulnerabilities without a fixed version or those 
# inherent to the base Debian/Python slim image that are under investigation.

# --- Example of OS-level vulnerabilities (Glibc / OpenSSL) ---
# CVE-2024-XXXX: Vulnerability in glibc that has no fix for Debian Bookworm yet.
# CVE-2023-YYYY: OpenSSL issue not reachable via AI Slop Gate CLI logic.

# --- Specific Ignored CVEs (based on your scan) ---

# node-tar: Arbitrary file creation (often found in Node-slim base)
# We ignore this because we don't use npm/node to extract untrusted archives.
CVE-2024-28863
CVE-2022-3517

# glob: Command Injection (found in node_modules of npm)
# CLI only uses node for internal execution, not for parsing user glob patterns via JS.
CVE-2022-3520

# cross-spawn: Regular expression denial of service
CVE-2024-21538

# --- Low/Medium noise ---
# You can also ignore by ID if you see specific library issues that are false positives